## Features

- **KPI cards**
  - Total Tickets, Open Tickets, Closed Tickets, Avg Resolution Time
- **Interactive tickets table**
  - Colored badges for _Status_ and _Priority_
  - Clean action buttons for edit/delete (UI only)
- **Filters**
  - Status, Priority, Department, Location
  - All filters update the table, KPIs, and chart in sync
- **Chart**
  - Bar chart: **Tickets by Status**, powered by Chart.js[web:681]
- **Agent performance section**
  - Simple list with tickets count and closed percentage
- **Responsive layout**
  - Table collapses into mobile‑friendly cards on small screens

---

## Tech Stack

- HTML5
- CSS3 (modular files: `base`, `header`, `cards`, `filters`, `table`, `agent`)
- Vanilla JavaScript
- Chart.js for the “Tickets by Status” bar chart

---

## Project Structure

```text
support-tickets-analytics-ui/
├─ index.html
└─ assets/
   ├─ css/
   │  ├─ base.css
   │  ├─ header.css
   │  ├─ cards.css
   │  ├─ filters.css
   │  ├─ table.css
   │  └─ agent.css
   ├─ images/
   │  ├─ dashboard-full.png
   │  └─ status-completed.png
   └─ js/
      └─ main.js
```

---

## Getting Started

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Eissa2123/support-tickets-analytics-ui.git
cd support-tickets-analytics-ui
# open index.html in your browser or use a local server (e.g. VS Code Live Server)
```

All data is mocked inside `assets/js/main.js` to keep the focus on UI, filtering logic, and KPI calculations.

